      "message": "Nope. The input blob is struct { uint8_t type; uint8_t req; ...}. But because the stm32 can only read it as an array of uint16_t\u0027s (the dedicated USB RAM is on the APB) and it\u0027s little-endian, that becomes encoded as 0x[\u003creq\u003e\u003ctype\u003e].\n\nThe Cr50\u0027s buffers and descriptors are all in program RAM, So this just avoids the byte-swapping and reads the struct as it really is.",
